WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.836
-Joe Biden had a big night
on Super Tuesday,

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:06.172
setting up a two-person
race with Bernie Sanders

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.540
for the Democratic nomination.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.809
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.413
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:17.583
It's worth remembering just how
high the stakes of this

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:20.453
Democratic primary are,
because right as Democrats

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.054
are deciding who
the nominee will be,

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:24.457
we're also dealing with a
national health emergency

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:27.127
over the spread of the
coronavirus and a president

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.928
who is totally unequipped
to handle it.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.464
Today, for example,
President Trump spoke

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.931
with reporters
at the White House

00:00:32.931 --> 00:00:35.535
about measures people can take
to prevent the spread

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.403
of the virus and said this.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:40.540
-We're always saying the common
sense of washing your hands,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.008
not touching your face.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.777
-I haven't touched
my face in weeks.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.180
In weeks.
I miss it.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.016
-Alright, first of all,
that can't be true

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.450
otherwise how did this happen?

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.587
I mean, if you didn't put all
that bronzer on your face,

00:00:55.587 --> 00:00:57.423
how did it get there?

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.959
It looks like he went to Sephora
for a free makeup tutorial

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.161
and it just went horribly wrong.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.196
Second,
I would just like to say,

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:06.332
you may not
have touched your face

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.601
but I would love
to touch your face,

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.237
just to see
what the texture is like.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:14.774
Is it like a sponge
or an old pancake?

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.508
When you press on it,
does it bounce back

00:01:16.508 --> 00:01:17.743
like a foam mattress?

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.513
Or did you get stuck
in place like silly putty?

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.615
I guess what I'm asking,
if I rolled your face

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.251
on a comic strip, would I be
able to see Calvin and Hobbs?

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.186
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.121
[ Applause ]

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:33.793
More importantly, there's been
a lack of widespread

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.695
national testing
for the coronavirus

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.730
in the United States compared
to other countries

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.065
due in large part to the Trump
administration's

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:41.767
lack of preparation
and the government's

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.069
slow and inept response.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.537
One expert called
it a national scandal,

00:01:45.537 --> 00:01:48.341
so you'll never guess
who Trump blamed it on today.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:51.911
-The Obama administration made a
decision on testing

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:55.214
that turned out to be very
detrimental to what we're doing.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:59.819
And we undid that decision a few
days ago so that the testing

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:03.356
can take place in a much more
accurate and rapid fashion.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.258
-He actually did it.
He found a way to blame

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.893
the coronavirus on Barack Obama.

00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:11.230
Dude, Obama's been out of office
for over three years. Let it go.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.067
the man's been wind surfing,
white water rafting,

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.202
and from the looks of him,
playing a Hollywood agent

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.603
in a remake of "Entourage."

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:19.906
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:23.009
You know, probably called
"Obamtourage."

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.111
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.480
Seriously, who's Trump going
to blame next? Hillary Clinton?

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.416
"I heard a rumor that one
of Hillary's missing e-mails

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:34.186
had the subject line 'Secret
plan to spread coronavirus.'"

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:36.388
Now, last night's results
were definitely surprising.

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:38.991
It seemed unlikely just a week
ago while Bernie Sanders,

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:41.026
who won the popular vote
in the first three states,

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:43.028
still managed to win big
delegate hulls

00:02:43.028 --> 00:02:44.263
in places like California.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.599
Joe Biden catapulted
from his huge victor

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.767
in South Carolina to win
blowouts in the South

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:51.970
and surprising victories in
places like Texas and Minnesota.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.873
And you could tell things
were going well for him

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.809
because when he took the stage
in L.A. to celebrate last night,

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.646
he was so giddy, he apparently
confused his wife

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.481
who was on his right with his
sister who was on his left.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:05.251
-By the way, this my little
sister, Valerie,

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.486
and I'm Jill's husband.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:07.987
Oh, no, no.
Wait a second.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.054
Oh, you switched on me.

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:11.090
This is my wife,
this is my sister.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.691
They switched on me.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:15.761
-Oh, boy, Joe!
Oh, boy.

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:19.131
You don't -- you never --
you never --

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:21.133
one of the first rules
of politics,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:24.937
you never want to confuse
your wife and your sister

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:28.975
unless you're starring
in a reality show on TLC.

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.377
Now, there are a lot
of takeaways

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.378
from the results last night,
but one thing I think

00:03:33.378 --> 00:03:35.881
we can enjoy is the fact that
ex-Republican billionaire

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:37.983
Mike Bloomberg had to drop out
today after spending

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:40.787
$500 million in an attempt
to buy the election.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.056
In the end, he only won one
contest

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.825
and it wasn't even in one
of the 50 states.

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:48.060
-A disappointing night
for Michael Bloomberg.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.630
He only won one territory,
American Samoa

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:55.434
and its four delegates despite
spending nearly $500 million.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:59.171
-That's right. He only won one
caucus in American Samoa.

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:02.075
These results were so bad
for Bloomberg he said "screw it"

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.010
and drank a Big Gulp
while smoking a cigarette

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.645
inside a bar.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:08.380
Bloomberg spent half
a billion dollars

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.550
and all he got was a nationally
televised atomic wedgie

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.019
from Elizabeth Warren
in the debates.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.688
And even though super Tuesday
didn't go the way she wanted,

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.091
we owe Warren a debt
of gratitude for single handedly

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.659
annihilating
the Bloomberg campaign.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.061
Elizabeth Warren devoured him
in those debates

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.796
like the T-Rex
from "Jurassic Park."

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.332
-I'd like to talk about
who we're running against,

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:30.002
a billionaire who calls
women fat broads

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.271
and horse-faced lesbians.

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.406
And, no, I'm not talking
about Donald Trump.

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:36.042
I'm talking
about Mayor Bloomberg.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:39.012
[ T-Rex screeches ]
-[ Screams ]

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:41.914
-And honestly --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:46.552
honestly I'm just shocked

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.254
he did so poorly
because Bloomberg

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:50.456
is such a talented
charismatic politician.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:53.659
Here he was yesterday on the
campaign trail busting out

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:57.130
some very advanced Spanish
during a Q&amp;A with reporters.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.565
-You spent a lot of time
in Texas.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:02.035
What'd you --
-Tehas we say here.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.602
-What'd you say?
-Tehas.

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:05.972
-Tehas?
-That's Spanish for Texas.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:06.939
-Okay.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:09.475
-[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:10.476
Oh, really.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.644
Is Tehas Spanish for Texas?

00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:14.414
Thanks a lot, Miguel.

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:15.748
That's Spanish for Michael.

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.383
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.985
So the short lived Bloomberg
experiment is now at the end

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:21.653
thanks in large part
to Elizabeth Warren.

00:05:21.653 --> 00:05:23.789
And now after
the Super Tuesday results,

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:24.857
the race is narrowed

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:26.392
to two candidates,
Biden and Sanders.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.793
And, for the voters
and the media,

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:29.662
there seems to be one
overwhelming

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.330
obsession in this race.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.999
A word you've heard
so many times

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.434
it probably haunts
you in your sleep.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:38.438
-Electability has been prized
by Democratic voters

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:40.740
over and above any policy issue.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:44.243
-The race clearly
is about electability.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:45.845
-Yes.
-This has the electability

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:46.746
since day one.

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.781
-The electability argument.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.282
-His electability argument.

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:51.818
-I have the electability case.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:53.252
-The electability question
of the evening.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.820
-It's about that electability.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.556
-People keep talking
about electability.

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.324
-All they're focused on
is electability.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:05:59.892
-Electability.
-Electability.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.928
-Electability.
-Electability.

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:05.164
-I'm pretty sure electability
is Wolf Blitzer's safe word,

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:08.167
which is interesting because
mine is Wolf Blitzer.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:12.038
Never had to use it,
and, honestly,

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.739
it's insane that we're still
talking about

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:15.942
electability three years
into the presidency

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:18.377
of the least electable person
in the history of elections.

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:20.579
I mean, Donald Trump is like
a lab experiment

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.915
where a bunch of scientists
got together and tried

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:25.384
to create the most
unelectable candidate possible.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:28.087
I mean, they combine the racism
of George Wallace

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.788
with the corruption
of Bernie Madoff,

00:06:29.788 --> 00:06:31.457
the trench coat of a mob boss,

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.726
and the tan line
of a Hairless Sphynx.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.828
[ Laughter and applause

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.429
The point is we have
no way of knowing

00:06:37.429 --> 00:06:38.530
who's the most electable.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.665
Just vote for whoever you think

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:40.799
would make the best president.

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:42.802
So now Democratic Party leaders

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:44.837
have rallied around Biden
as the supposedly

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:46.772
electable alternative
to Bernie Sanders.

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:49.542
Several former candidates came
out in the waning hours

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:52.111
before Super Tuesday
to close ranks around Biden.

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:54.513
And at a rally for Biden
in Texas, former Congressman

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:57.850
Beto O'Rourke even busted out
some of his trademark Spanish.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.119
-We have now seen,
even in just the last 24 hours,

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:02.154
this cascade of critical
endorsements

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:04.123
coming to back Joe Biden
in what has amounted

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:06.725
to a really rapid reset
in this race.

00:07:06.725 --> 00:07:09.895
Just in the last day,
more than 125 endorsements.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:12.765
-Today I am ending my campaign

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:16.836
and endorsing Joe Biden
for president.

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:22.041
-I'm delighted to endorse and
support Joe Biden for president.

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:26.045
-On behalf of every one
of the 254 counties

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:29.681
of this great state,
we welcome Dr. Jill Biden

00:07:29.681 --> 00:07:33.085
and Vice President Joe Biden,
el próximo presidente

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:37.356
de los Estados Unidos aquí
con nosotros este momento.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.425
-And I guess it'd make sense
Beto would bust out

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:41.593
some Spanish, because after all
he was in...

00:07:41.593 --> 00:07:43.296
-Tehas.
-So...

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:46.265
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:47.833
The so-called moderates --

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.868
[ Applause ]

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:52.071
the so-called moderates
in the party joined forces

00:07:52.071 --> 00:07:54.707
to stop Bernie, which prompted
cable news pundits

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.475
to lead on any relevant

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:58.343
pop culture reference
they could think of.

00:07:58.343 --> 00:08:00.546
First CNN tried a riff
on "The Avengers."

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:01.848
-What we saw last night
is something

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:03.849
I have to say
I have never seen before.

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:07.186
This sea of endorsements
by former candidates

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:09.288
all at the last minute
before a key day.

00:08:09.288 --> 00:08:11.223
Pete Buttigieg, Amy Klobuchar,
Beto O'Rourke,

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:13.125
all endorsing Joe Biden.

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:16.595
-It was the great moderate
Avengers coming together.

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:18.464
-Political Avengers.
-Who cares about the --

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:19.832
Yeah, we're talking about
"Avengers."

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.634
It was all of them
combined together

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:22.835
to get the stones from Thanos.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:23.936
I thought Thanos was Trump,

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.504
but apparently
it's Bernie Sanders.

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:27.873
-Alright, first of all, Bernie
is definitely not Thanos.

00:08:27.873 --> 00:08:29.842
Second, if the moderates
are the Avengers,

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.777
that would make Joe Biden
Chris Evans

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:33.379
at the end of "Endgame."

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.147
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.649
And then there were Republican
pundits like former Bush

00:08:37.649 --> 00:08:39.785
administration official
and Iraq war champion

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:42.221
David Frum who used this
insulting analogy

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:44.890
to describe the difference
between Biden and Bernie voters.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:48.059
-Joe Biden appeals to people
who pay their cable bills

00:08:48.059 --> 00:08:49.261
on the day it arrives.

00:08:49.261 --> 00:08:51.563
Bernie Sanders appeals
to people who may forget

00:08:51.563 --> 00:08:53.098
to pay their cable bill
entirely.

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:54.467
-Alright,
not only is that insulting,

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:56.702
but also who needs cable
anymore? Just cut the cord.

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:59.371
You know, personally all I watch
is Netflix, HBO

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:00.972
and none of the adult channels.

00:09:00.972 --> 00:09:04.242
Although Hustler TV does have
a great election coverage

00:09:04.242 --> 00:09:06.479
on their political roundtable
show "Erect-ability."

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:09.715
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:12.418
[ Applause ]

00:09:16.022 --> 00:09:19.291
And then CNN tried a different
analogy to offer perspective

00:09:19.291 --> 00:09:21.660
from the Bernie side by citing
"Star Wars."

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.364
-I'm hearing a lot of joy
and also a lot of pain from,

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:26.865
you know,
different sets of friends.

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:30.302
On the one hand, I think there's
a joy that there has been

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:32.371
this consolidation
for the moderate lane.

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:35.440
But on the other hand, you do
have another set of Democrats

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.243
who feel like this
is the Empire striking back.

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:39.412
-I'm not sure I'd describe
the moderates as the Empire.

00:09:39.412 --> 00:09:41.080
If you gave Joe Biden
a lightsaber,

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.015
he'd immediately
cut his own leg off

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.217
and make a bunch
of dad jokes about it.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:47.219
"How'd I do that?
Well, I'm stumped.

00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:48.520
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.489
My wife liked it.
Oh, my sister."

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:52.391
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.391 --> 00:09:54.993
So the race is now dramatically
changed from where it was

00:09:54.993 --> 00:09:57.262
just one week ago
with Biden ahead of Bernie

00:09:57.262 --> 00:09:58.497
by about 50 delegates.

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:00.833
As we tape this,
it's now a two-person race

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:02.535
with a clear contrast
between the moderate

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:03.969
and progressive wings
of the party.

00:10:03.969 --> 00:10:05.604
And no matter who gets
the nomination,

00:10:05.604 --> 00:10:07.439
they'll be going up against
a guy who's biggest

00:10:07.439 --> 00:10:09.308
accomplishment
in three years is this.

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:11.610
-I haven't touched
my face in weeks.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.245
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:13.245 --> 00:10:16.148
[ Cheers and applause ]

